apture verification logic. I've realized that the failure list needs updating to include \"casi,\" the Spanish for \"almost.\" Moreover, I'm adding \"captur\" to the success list, because it is needed for many languages. I am wondering why this was not a problem before.\n\n\n**Interpreting Capture Failure**\n\nI'm now interpreting the capture failure, and it looks like \"me para\" translates to \"it stops the capture process\". I'm also seeing a pattern in the logs, such as when the Pokemon is at low health and asleep. The `time.sleep` in `_press` may be the culprit. I am wondering why the menu isn't always detected. When the ball breaks, the Pokemon wakes up, and attacks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Get-Content src/bot_main.py | Select-String -Context 0, 15 \\\"def is_hp_low\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Brian\\\\Desktop\\\\workspace\\\\pizzant\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking is_hp_low\"","toolSummary":"\"Read is_hp_low in bot_main.py\""}}]}
